    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1710.05468_rag::chunk_011</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1905.10854_rag::chunk_012</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceChunk rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">JMLRdropout_rag::chunk_007</hasEvidenceChunk>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Deep neural nets with a large number of parameters are very powerful machine learning systems.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The equations used for computing the forward pass in a neural net with two hidden layers and one output layer, each constituting a module through which one can backpropagate gradients.</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">neural network classication eciency scales linearly with the size of the network</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">training a neural network with dropout can be seen as training a collection of 2 n thinned networks</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We start by studying a neural network with one hidden layer of 100 neurons</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The feed-forward operation of a standard neural network (Figure 3a) can be described as</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">scaling down the weights of the trained neural network</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">interesting structure which the neural network can capture</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The NNs are trained to discriminate points sampled from two largely overlapping Gaussian distributions</hasEvidenceText>
    <hasEvidenceText rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">We trained dropout neural networks for classication problems on data sets in dierent domains.</hasEvidenceText>
  </rdf:Description>
